From 9e200920c84b862bba60c4e715be63e4784ed16d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Amadeusz Starzykiewicz <megawebmaster@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 12:37:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(split): forward central status to peripherals

Adds a SET_PERIPHERAL_STATUS central command carrying the active layer, the
peripheral battery levels, the selected endpoint and BLE profile state, and WPM,
so a peripheral carrying a display can render them. Previously the only payload
travelling central to peripheral was the HID indicator state, which left a
display-carrying peripheral with no way to show anything beyond its own battery.

Layer and endpoint changes are broadcast immediately; battery levels and WPM ride
a periodic tick (CONFIG_ZMK_SPLIT_PERIPHERAL_STATUS_INTERVAL_S, default 60s) to
avoid a BLE write per second. A broadcast is also triggered when a peripheral's
characteristics are discovered, so a peripheral that reboots does not wait out the
interval with stale data.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Cr1KsAvQhNX7c2DwkXyu8j
